RKNN-Toolkit2 version: 2.3.2
Target platform: rk3588
Date: 2026-08-20

The PDF labels are GGML formats.  The following calls were made against the
official aarch64 CPython 3.12 wheel inside an isolated Linux container:

  RKNN.config(target_platform="rk3588", quantized_dtype=LABEL)

LABEL                       RESULT
q8_0                        rejected: invalid quantized_dtype
q5_0                        rejected: invalid quantized_dtype
q4_K                        rejected: invalid quantized_dtype
q4_0                        rejected: invalid quantized_dtype
w8a8                        accepted (return code 0)
asymmetric_quantized-8      accepted (return code 0; alias for the native INT8 path)
w8a16                       rejected: not supported on rk3588
w4a16                       rejected: not supported on rk3588
w16a16i                     accepted (return code 0; integer FP16-equivalent path)
w16a16i_dfp                 accepted (return code 0; integer FP16-equivalent path)

Toolkit2 reported its accepted quantized_dtype vocabulary as:
  w8a8, w8a16, w16a16i, w16a16i_dfp, w4a16

The important distinction is that native w8a8 is not GGML q8_0: it quantizes
activations as well as weights and requires a representative calibration
dataset.  No numeric row may therefore be relabeled from q8_0 to w8a8.  The
three PDF 4/5-bit modes have no native RK3588 graph-conversion counterpart in
Toolkit2 2.3.2.  The toolkit's distinct w8a16 and w4a16 modes are both rejected
for RK3588; neither can be used as a weight-only substitute.
